Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:23:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 124/159] [ae-patch] Read Claude Code's per-model effort levels
 for the default effort

Claude Code 2.1.304 keeps effort per model, as modelSettings[<model id>]
.effortLevel in settings.json, so a file with no top-level effortLevel made
every session's label "none" and the Effort menu said "Claude default"
while Opus ran at high. The runner now records the top-level level under
"*" and each model's own level under its id, as a small JSON label, and the
menu picks the entry for the session's current model.
